{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>When a woman brings forth seed.</b> After he completed the law of pure and impure in foods, he mentioned the impurity of a person and began with the woman who gives birth, for birth is the beginning. And many say that the woman emits seed first, she gives birth to a male — therefore 'and she bears a male,' and therefore the opinion of the sages of Greece is that the seed belongs to the woman, and the seed of the male coagulates, and all the son is from the blood of the woman. Now the meaning of תזריע: she gives seed, for she is like the earth." "The vav of <b>and she shall be impure</b> is like a weak kaf peh alef [in the language of Ishmael]. And the cause of her impurity for seven days is until she returns to the quadrilateral, and likewise it is found in the days of illness, for the change is visible until the end of seven [days]." "<b>Her menstrual impurity.</b> A noun in the pattern of בזת, and both of them are from doubled-root verbs." "<b>Her illness.</b> Its meaning is like חולי, like מדוה מצרים, for the blood that goes out is an illness in the flesh of the woman."], :book :leviticus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 12, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:09:43.296054760Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}